<title>GERMANY: German rapeseed, barley damaged but may recover.</title>
<headline>German rapeseed, barley damaged but may recover.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH, Germany 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freezing weather over the past two weeks damaged some German winter rapeseed and barley, a DWD meteorological institute official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The official stressed that damage was not widespread and ws unlikely to be very serious if temperatures rose as predicted.</p>
<p>Plants might well be able to recover in the spring.</p>
<p>&quot;Temperatures are now recovering...snow cover is still intact in many areas so it is hard to gauge the extent of the damage,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
